<</E(  Both slicing/string-method validation and a full regular-expression match take O\(L\) time for a string of length L. The slicing approach makes each field boundary explicit and is easy to teach and debug. A regular expression is compact and useful when the format becomes more complicated, but a reader may need to understand regex syntax before safely changing the rule. The normalised string requires O\(L\) space because upper\(\) and replace\(\) create new strings. )/K[ 1]/P 122 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S/H2/T(  Both slicing/string-method validation and a full regular-expression match take O\(L\) time for a string of length L. The slicing approach makes each field boundary explicit and is easy to teach and debug. A regular expression is compact and useful when the format becomes more complicated, but a reader may need to understand regex syntax before safely changing the rule. The normalised string requires O\(L\) space because upper\(\) and replace\(\) create new strings. )/Type/StructElem>>
