<</E(Alocal name exists inside its function. A global name is defined at module level. A nonlocal name refers to a variable in the nearest enclosing function scope, not the global scope. The global keyword is required when assigning to a module- level variable inside a function; without it, Python treats the assigned name as local. Global mutation is usually avoided because it creates hidden dependencies and makes testing and debugging harder. Passing values as arguments and returning results is generally clearer. )/K[ 3]/P 126 0 R /Pg 22 0 R /S/H2/T(Alocal name exists inside its function. A global name is defined at module level. A nonlocal name refers to a variable in the nearest enclosing function scope, not the global scope. The global keyword is required when assigning to a module- level variable inside a function; without it, Python treats the assigned name as local. Global mutation is usually avoided because it creates hidden dependencies and makes testing and debugging harder. Passing values as arguments and returning results is generally clearer. )/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
