<</E(The objective is achieved: the redesigned algorithms preserve correctness while reducing repeated work from exponential to linear. Memoisation is a major improvement over naive recursion, but the iterative solution is the strongest deployment choice for n up to 1,000 because it avoids recursion depth and uses O\(1\) auxiliary space. The original naive version remains useful only for demonstrating the recurrence on very small inputs. Memoisation remains useful when a recursive formulation is easier to understand or when subproblems are not naturally processed in a simple bottom-up order. )/K[ 7]/P 133 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
