1459 0 obj
<</Dest[ 18 0 R /Fit]/Next 1460 0 R /Parent 1448 0 R /Title(Both slicing/string-method validation and a full regular-expression match take O\(L\) time for a string of length L. The slicing approach makes each field boundary explicit and is easy to teach and debug. A regular expression is compact and useful when the format becomes more complicated, but a reader may need to understand regex syntax before safely changing the rule. The normalised string requires O\(L\) space because upper\(\) and replace\(\) create new strings.)>>
endobj
